# cobra 0.31.1, numpy 1.26.4 -- reading, gapfilling and solving genome-scale models.
#
# NO `container:` LINE, AND THAT IS NOT AN OMISSION. The image is `docker/cobra/`, built
# by `docker/cobra/dev.sh --build` and NOT pushed. Naming an unpublished image here points
# every solve at a registry entry that does not exist, and it fails at stage time on
# whichever host drew the task rather than in front of whoever caused it -- which is the
# same trade `resources/env/ecspr.env` documents. `conda: build-refs-cobra` is the working
# route until someone pushes the image; the `container:` line goes in AFTER the push and
# not before.
#
# The four kbase modelling transforms were run against the local build in curation round 5
# by temporarily naming `docker://cobra:local` here -- see research/kbase/curation/r5.
#
# numpy<2 is why this cannot merge into `python_for_data_science`: cobra's optlang stack
# needs it and polars needs numpy>=2.
conda: build-refs-cobra
